VALUES ('65,000 JOBS POSSIBLE FROM SOCIAL/COMMUNITY ENTERPRISES – REPORT', '65000-jobs-possible-from-social-community-enterprises-report', '<p><a href="https://4.bp.blogspot.com/_cgq3tUEQMDo/TDIkPOLPifI/AAAAAAAAAGM/iT--UljnIws/s1600/At+the+official+launch+of+the+Task+Force+Report+on+Social+Enterprise+June+2010+HALF+A+MB.JPG"><img decoding="async" src="https://4.bp.blogspot.com/_cgq3tUEQMDo/TDIkPOLPifI/AAAAAAAAAGM/iT--UljnIws/s320/At+the+official+launch+of+the+Task+Force+Report+on+Social+Enterprise+June+2010+HALF+A+MB.JPG" border="0" alt="" /></a><br /><span ><span >Community and social enterprise projects, if driven by the Government &#8211; could provide up to 65,000 jobs nationally, according to a report published in June, 2010, by the Task Force on Social Enterprise. <a href="https://changingireland.ie/SocialCommunityEnterprise.html">You can download the full 16-page report here.</a></span></span></p>
<div><span ><span >Read more on social enterprises on pages 19-21 of &#8216;Changing Ireland&#8217; Issue 32 which features examples from Ireland, England and Scotland. As of now, that issue (our latest) is <a href="https://changingireland.ie/">on our homepage.</a></span></span></div>
<div><span >Check out our upcoming Summer edition from more on Social and Community Enterprise &#8211; from how it should create jobs, to interviews with people working in Speedpak, a social enterprise company in north Dublin.</span></div>', 'Community and social enterprise projects, if driven by the Government – could provide up to 65,000 jobs nationally, according to a report published in June, 2010, by the Task Force on Social Enterprise. You can download the full 16-page report here. Read more on social enterprises on pages 19-21 of ‘Changing Ireland’ Issue 32 which', '', '', '[{"slug":"uncategorized","title":"Uncategorized"}]', '[]', '', 345, 1, '2010-07-05T18:13:00Z', '2010-07-05T18:13:00Z', '2010-07-05T18:13:00Z')
